					<p class="body1" align="left"><span class="body1 style73"> <h2>News archive</h2><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-09-14 | Friday</font></strong><br><br>ohshitsun!<br /><br />a mid-week download?  why, that&#39;s crazy.  not as crazy as this track that you&#39;re about to peep tho.  everytime i&#39;m in the car with <strong>Khalil</strong>, i learn something new.  one minute we&#39;re talkin about some gangster shit, the next he&#39;s tellin me about some town music.  well here you go.<br /><br />today&#39;s cut is:<br /><br /><u><strong><a href="http://www.masslinemedia.com/mp3/Suntonio%20Banadanaz%20-%20Meditate%20(feat.%20Abyssinian%20Creole).mp3">Suntonio Bandanaz - &quot;Meditate&quot; (feat. Abyssinian Creole / produced by Phreewil)</a></strong></u><br /><br />The album is called <strong>&quot;Who Iz Suntonio Bandanaz?!&quot;</strong> and it also features <strong>SKIM</strong>, <strong>Macklemore</strong>, <strong>Kas1</strong>, <strong>Julie C.</strong>, <strong>Daichi Sawa &amp; Rufio</strong>, with production from <strong>WD4D</strong>, <strong>Audeos</strong>, <strong>DJ 100Proof</strong>, <strong>Phreewil</strong>, <strong>Dead Noise </strong>&amp;<strong> Blake</strong>.<br /><br />check Asun&#39;s myspace page: 




<u><strong><a href="http://www.myspace.com/bandanaz4u">http://www.myspace.com/bandanaz4u</a>



</strong></u><br /><br />i&#39;m connected to each of the folks on this track in an interesting way.  <strong>Gabriel</strong> lives a 3 blocks from me, <strong>Khingz</strong> used to live three blocks from me, Phreewil and I were roommates for three days back in 2001, and i&#39;m guessing that <strong>Asun</strong> has crashed at the cribs of each of these folks at least three times.  <br /><br />ain&#39;t the town a trip!<br /><br />saba<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-09-13 | Thursday</font></strong><br><br><div>&quot;featuring Geologic (of Blue Scholars)&quot;</div><div><br /></div>Yes, I do actually rap on beats produced by people who are not named <strong>Sabzi</strong>. And yes, I&#39;d be down to get on a track with you under either or both conditions: 1. you&#39;re the homie and/or I dig your shit or 2. monetary compensation! And no, Mr. Myspace Producer, Blue Scholars does not need additional production.<br /><br />Saba&#39;s already banging out beats that are giving birth to whatever the new BS album will sound like. In the meantime, I&#39;m writing like a madman. I&#39;m even writing songs <em>in my head</em> (a la Jay-Z, Lil Weezy and <strong>Thig Natural from the Physics</strong>). Here are some collabs that came out this year:<br /><br /><strong>Language Arts ft. Geologic - Exclusive&nbsp;</strong>(prod. by Def Dee)<a href="http://www.myspace.com/deflanguage"></a><div><a href="http://www.myspace.com/deflanguage">myspace.com/deflanguage</a><br /><br /><strong>Grynch ft. Geologic &amp; Portia - Summertime&nbsp;</strong>(prod. by Udi)<a href="http://www.myspace.com/grynchmusic"></a></div><div><a href="http://www.myspace.com/grynchmusic">myspace.com/grynchmusic</a><br /><br /><strong>Orbitron (Circle of Fire Crew) ft. Geologic - Freedom Song&nbsp;</strong>(prod. by Alonzo aka &quot;Big Zo&quot;)<a href="http://www.myspace.com/BeaconSkillz"></a></div><div><a href="http://www.myspace.com/BeaconSkillz">myspace.com/BeaconSkillz</a><br /><br /><strong>Bambu ft. Geologic, Kiwi &amp; DJ Kuttin Kandi - Home Cooked&nbsp;</strong>(prod. by Steez)<a href="http://profile.myspace.com/index.cfm?fuseaction=user.viewprofile&amp;friendid=124985842"></a></div><div><a href="http://profile.myspace.com/index.cfm?fuseaction=user.viewprofile&amp;friendid=124985842">myspace.com/steezstrumentalz</a></div><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-09-11 | Tuesday</font></strong><br><br><div><br /></div><div><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px"><strong>Kanye West</strong> or <strong>50 Cent</strong>? Six years after the event that ushered in a new era of martial-law-on-the-low and this is the best distraction they can come up with? (There&#39;s some FIRE on that <strong><em>Graduation</em></strong> album, though. As for <strong><em>Curtis</em></strong>... ehhhh.)&nbsp;</p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; min-height: 14px; margin: 0px">&nbsp;</p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px">As the hype monster continues to feed itself manufactured beef, I&#39;ma cast my soundscan vote today for... <strong>GRAYSKUL.</strong>&nbsp;That&#39;s right - the new album&nbsp;<strong><em>Bloody Radio</em></strong> drops today as well and every fan of quality NW hip-hop would do right to pass up on the hype monster and cop the <strong>Oldominion</strong> fams&#39; new Rhymesayers release. Plus, I heard that both Fiddy AND Kanye said they&#39;ll retire if <em>Bloody Radio</em> outsells <em>Graduation</em> and <em>Curtis</em>. Anything&#39;s possible right?</p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; min-height: 14px; margin: 0px">&nbsp;</p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px">Cop that shit.</p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px">Geo</p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px">&nbsp;</p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px">----</p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px">&nbsp;</p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px"><span style="font-family: arial; font-size: 11px" class="Apple-style-span"><span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">September 11, 2007</span></span><span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span"><br /></span></p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px"><span style="font-family: arial; font-size: 11px" class="Apple-style-span"><span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">GRAYSKUL - BLOODY RADIO Album Release party</span></span></p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px"><span style="font-family: arial; font-size: 11px" class="Apple-style-span">feat.</span></p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px"><span style="font-family: arial; font-size: 11px" class="Apple-style-span">Mr. Lif</span></p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px"><span style="font-family: arial; font-size: 11px" class="Apple-style-span">Eligh &amp; Lucky I Am of Living Legends</span></p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px"><span style="font-family: arial; font-size: 11px" class="Apple-style-span">Macklemore &amp; Xperience (Step Cousins)</span></p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px"><span style="font-family: arial; font-size: 11px" class="Apple-style-span">DJ blesOne \\ Hosted By Grieves</span></p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px"><span style="font-family: arial; font-size: 11px" class="Apple-style-span">SEATTLE, WA | @&nbsp;Chop Suey<br />Address - 1325 E. Madison<br />Ages - all ages + Bar w/ I.D<br />8PM | $12&nbsp;<br /><a style="font-family: arial, helvetica; color: #751e00; font-size: 11px; font-weight: normal; text-decoration: none" href="http://www.ticketweb.com/" target="_blank">www.TicketWeb.com</a><br /><a style="font-family: arial, helvetica; color: #751e00; font-size: 11px; font-weight: normal; text-decoration: none" href="http://www.ObeseProductions.com/" target="_blank">www.ObeseProductions.com</a>&nbsp;</span></p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px">&nbsp;</p></div><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-09-11 | Tuesday</font></strong><br><br>on Sunday, i went out to kick for the afternoon with my guy <strong>Khalil (Khingz)</strong> and our homie <strong>Jill</strong>.  he came thru the crib and was like &quot;ey foo, i hella heard that there&#39;s this <strong>sneaker expo</strong> in <strong>Kirkland</strong> goin on today.&quot;<br /> <img src="http://www.masslinemedia.com/images/kirkland/blog1.jpg" alt="" /><br /><br />word? let&#39;s go check it out.  we grabbed some coffee and made the trek out to <strong>Peter Kirk Park</strong> in Kirkland.  <br /><br />Khalil kept talkin about how whenever he goes anywhere north or east of Seattle he gets nervous.  i told him to chill.  <br /><br />Kirkland isn&#39;t a bad place.  it&#39;s actually kinda crackin. hella parks, stores, community center for young folks to kick it. etc.  i went to many a <strong>GLITTA</strong> by <strong>Sonny Bonoho</strong> and <strong>Unexpected Arrival</strong> shows at the community center in Kirkland not long ago.<br /><br />anyway, when we showed up at the park we couldn&#39;t find any kind of sneaker expo.  we looked in windows of the community center and saw nothing.  nobody in the parking lot either. just this guy playing the bag pipes.<br /><br /> <img src="http://www.masslinemedia.com/images/kirkland/kirk4.jpg" alt="" /><br /><br />ey khalil, what kind of shoes were they expo-ing again?<br /><br /> <img src="http://www.masslinemedia.com/images/kirkland/kirk3.jpg" alt="" /><br /><br />then out of the corner of his eye, Khalil was like &quot;hey those look like some sneaker head doods over there.&quot;  and he was right.  they did look like sneaker head doods.  they were hella wearing sneakers, and they were all doods.<br /><br /> <img src="http://www.masslinemedia.com/images/kirkland/kirk2.jpg" alt="" /><br /><br />turns out this &quot;sneaker expo&quot; was really just <strong>33 pairs of sneakers laid out on a picnic table</strong>.  ironically, i found out i knew the guy that put it together. he goes by <strong>Derrick</strong> and i met him through my old roommate and homie <strong>Hoven</strong> (brother of <strong>Darvin</strong> of <strong>PFOM</strong>, <strong>TIKKKI</strong> show at BLVD, and the graphic artist behind <strong>Lovework</strong>.)<br /><br /> <img src="http://www.masslinemedia.com/images/kirkland/kirk1.jpg" alt="" /><br /><br />Derrick and his homies Tony, Emmanuel, and Lenard were proud to present the first annual <strong>Feet &amp; Greet </strong>at the Peter Kirk Park in Kirkland.  i actually thought it was kinda filthy, especially after coming from MAGIC in Vegas where the cool guy snobbery was a little overwhelming.  these were just some good town folks enjoying some drinks and sneakers on a late summer afternoon.  <br /><br />keep doin yo&#39; thing fellas!<br /><br />we stayed just lampin for a minute and dipped.  later on, i got home and laughed at how most of the pictures we took usually had Khalil walking away in them.<br /><br />saba<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-09-10 | Monday</font></strong><br><br><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px">Folks who don&#39;t know have been asking, and folks who know have been saying. You might have seen and heard my dude <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">Language Arts</span> at a recent <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">Gabriel Teodros</span> set, or most recently with Good Medicine (at Capitol Hill Block Party) or at the surprise Blue Scholars set at Bumbershoot last week.</p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; min-height: 14px; margin: 0px">&nbsp;</p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px">I&#39;ve had the privilege off seeing the homie LA hold it down at various open-mics and sidewalk ciphers around the town over the years. The cat is formidable with the speech, from <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">Youth Speaks</span> to his work with <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">Rajnii Eddins</span> (as Truth &amp; Knowledge). He recently won the <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">PUSH MC Battle</span> earlier this year and believe me - putting money on the other dude is the best way to turn a dollar into fifteen cents.&nbsp;</p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; min-height: 14px; margin: 0px">&nbsp;</p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px">I&#39;ve hit the studio a couple times with LA and got a chance to preview some of his work with producer&nbsp;<span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">Def Dee</span>. These cats are working on a couple of projects together, and I don&#39;t mean to blow their spot even before they get a chance to drop the album - but the shit is FILTHY. Every track is a nod to the true school, but very much focused on the present and future.</p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; min-height: 14px; margin: 0px">&nbsp;</p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px">Oh, did I mention I did a track with LA and Def? You can peep the track (&quot;Exclusive&quot;) on their myspace page right here: <a href="http://www.myspace.com/deflanguage" target="new">myspace.com/deflanguage</a>.</p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px">&nbsp;</p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px">peace</p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px">Geo</p><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><center><div class="pagenumbers"><A HREF="archive.php?from=80">[&lt;&lt;]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=0">[1]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=5">[2]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=10">[3]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=15">[4]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=20">[5]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=25">[6]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=30">[7]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=35">[8]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=40">[9]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=45">[10]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=50">[11]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=55">[12]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=60">[13]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=65">[14]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=70">[15]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=75">[16]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=80">[17]</A> [18] <A HREF="archive.php?from=90">[19]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=95">[20]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=100">[21]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=105">[22]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=110">[23]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=115">[24]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=120">[25]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=125">[26]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=130">[27]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=135">[28]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=140">[29]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=145">[30]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=150">[31]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=155">[32]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=160">[33]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=165">[34]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=170">[35]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=175">